==English==

===Etymology===
1935, [[American English]]; from ''[[icky-boo]]'' (circa 1920): [[sickly]], [[nauseated]]; [[baby talk]] corruption of '''[[sick]]'''; from a sentimental term for [[Jazz]] music.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɪki/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-icky.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪki|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[unpleasant]]ly [[sticky]]; [[yucky]]; [[disgusting]]
#: ''I stepped in something '''icky''' and it smells terrible.''
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[excessively]] [[sentimental]]

